  "statuses_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/MiniMax-AI/OpenAgentCore/statuses/e01726b2601dd72019f1160b348d571102923f7d",
  "number": 808,
  "state": "closed",
  "locked": false,
  "title": "Reuse finished Environment preparation across Sessions",
  "user": {
    "login": "SaladDay",
    "id": 92240037,
    "node_id": "U_kgDOBX94pQ",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92240037?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/SaladDay",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SaladDay/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "## What users see\n\nCore may start a hosted Environment from the result of an earlier preparation in the same Project whose effective configuration, after Template composition, is identical, for up to 24 hours after that preparation. Each Session still gets its own copy. Setup commands and package installation then do not run again for this Session. Only `/environment` is reused; HOME and other compute-local changes are not. Setup must not create per-Session unique values, perform external side effects that must happen per Session, or fetch credentials that expire within 24 hours; configurations that need this must differ (for example in `env` or `files`). Providers that do not declare the operations (Docker, E2B) always prepare in full. There is no setting, no `/v1` or OpenAPI change and no management API.\n\n## Key\n\nSHA-256 hex of: the tenant ID, then each initial file's (path, sha256 of body), then each setup operation's request (JSON) and sha256 of its data. It excludes Environment, Session, Harness and Agent. Network policy is not part of it: preparation always uses the host network and Core rejects non-enabled effective network for Sessions. Core never interprets the key beyond computing it.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Provider protocol: two optional operations, `RestorePreparation(ref, key) (bool, error)` and `SavePreparation(ref, key)`, declared Supported or Unsupported together in each adapter's operations file. Both address the initial compute, because compute state is empty until initialization completes. Docker and E2B declare Unsupported.\n- Node wire: `restore_preparation` (`key` -> `restored`) and `save_preparation` (`key`), both fields added to the strict frame decoder (`generation_json.go`) with a round-trip test. Protocol version unchanged; the fields are additive.\n- Core worker (`runtime_preparation_cache.go`, `runtime_initialization.go`): a hit skips the file and setup operations but still sends `finalize`; a miss prepares and then saves; a save error is logged and does not fail the Session; a restore error fails preparation.\n- microsandbox helper (`preparation.go`): all storage, TTL and seeding. One tar archive of `initialization`, `packages` and `workspace` under `/environment` (never `runtime-state`, which holds the running daemon's Codex home, Claude SDK history and completion markers) per (key, image digest, workspace mode) in a private directory under the Runtime home, valid 24 hours, pruned past the TTL and then oldest first above 8 GiB. The bound exists because the TTL alone does not limit disk on a busy node; a measured archive is tens of MiB (51 MiB real, 200 MiB synthetic), so 8 GiB holds over a hundred. Owned disk goes through guest tar and the SDK file copy; an NFS bind goes through host tar with xattrs preserved. An entry that fails to extract is deleted, so only that Session fails. The save gets at most half of the remaining preparation budget, so it never takes the time completion needs.\n- Daemon: finalize rebinds the restored `installed.json` identity to the current Session when the selection hash is identical, and still rejects a different selection. One existing test that expected an identity-only mismatch to fail now uses a changed selection.\n- Docs in English and Chinese: Environments \"Preparation reuse\", the Provider protocol, and the node generation protocol.\n\n## Measured\n\nCopy throughput (mx2, real Environment: 51 MiB, about 320 files, one 47 MiB binary):\n- Owned disk, inside the guest: save about 0.4 s; restore 0.47 s copy in + 0.20 s extract + 0.09 s sync.\n- NFS bind, inside the guest: restore 1.09 s + 8.17 s, rejected as too slow. On the host: save 0.14 s, extract 0.65 s, works while the guest runs, owner and mode kept. This is the implemented path.\n\nEnd to end on mx (fresh install of e01726b2, microsandbox node mx2 with NFS workspace storage, one Template with an npm package, a setup command, an initial file, a Skill and env):\n\n| Session | Harness | Result | restore / save ms | create to ready s | create to first text s |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| S1 | codex | miss, saved | 90 / 152 | 31.1 | 33.5 |\n| S2 | codex | hit | 315 / none | 12.3 | 14.8 |\n| S3 | claude_sdk | hit | 255 / none | 18.2 | 22.2 |\n| S4 | codex, one env value changed | miss, saved | 89 / 152 | 21.8 | 26.8 |\n| S5 | codex, S1 entry aged 25 h | miss, saved again | 90 / 149 | 22.9 | 33.8 |\n\nEvery Turn saw the package, the setup output, the initial file and the Skill. The store is 0700 with 0600 entries owned by the node user, and an entry holds only `initialization/`, `packages/` and `workspace/`. Hosted regression: codex 9/9 and claude_sdk 9/9. The first e2e run (b336d803) found the strict frame decoder rejecting the new fields; fixed in e01726b2.\n\n## Tests\n\nCore: hit, miss and failed save. Daemon: finalize rebinds an identical restored installation and rejects a different selection. Helper: an expired entry is not restored. Node: preparation request and response frames survive strict decoding. Failure paths (failed extract, save budget) were not exercised on a real VM.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/MiniMax-AI/codesmith/OpenAgentCore/pr/808?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795171761&installation_model_id=427615&pr_number=808&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=MiniMax-AI%2FOpenAgentCore&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FMiniMax-AI%2FOpenAgentCore%2Fpull%2F808&signature=5ca58f88eee7b614522d351e46efd43c49ac50eaa6ca81d02b4908671310aee2\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n",
